(One buffer passed as two parameters and appended to itself: the append
 grows the buffer, which can move it, and reads what it appends from the
 moved buffer.)
To 'merge' of a buffer called first and a buffer called second.
    append second to first.
    Print "first {first's size} second {second's size}".

a buffer called hold is "abc".
For each number from 1 to 400, append "abcdefgh" to hold.
'merge' of hold and hold.
Print "hold {hold's size}".
